WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.350 --> 00:00:05.884
Hello, everyone! I'm Ms. Emma. Welcome to Online Cambodia Grade twelve English.

2
00:00:06.184 --> 00:00:09.547
Hi! I'm Visal. Let's learn together!

3
00:00:09.847 --> 00:00:17.515
Unit three: Passive Voice in All Tenses. Today you will change active sentences to passive and use them in exams.

4
00:00:17.815 --> 00:00:20.456
Here is our lesson map. Let's start!

5
00:00:21.400 --> 00:00:24.412
Part one: words. You will learn eight new words.

6
00:00:25.250 --> 00:00:26.065
Passive.

7
00:00:27.050 --> 00:00:29.618
Passive means with the object as the subject.

8
00:00:30.217 --> 00:00:31.810
This sentence is passive.

9
00:00:32.417 --> 00:00:34.663
Your turn. Say: Passive.

10
00:00:37.500 --> 00:00:38.257
Passive.

11
00:00:39.017 --> 00:00:39.774
Agent.

12
00:00:40.783 --> 00:00:43.178
Agent means the person who does the action.

13
00:00:43.783 --> 00:00:45.446
The agent is the teacher.

14
00:00:46.050 --> 00:00:48.238
Your turn. Say: Agent.

15
00:00:51.100 --> 00:00:51.880
Agent.

16
00:00:52.617 --> 00:00:53.351
Built.

17
00:00:54.350 --> 00:00:56.837
Built means past participle of build.

18
00:00:57.450 --> 00:00:59.972
The bridge was built in 2005.

19
00:01:00.583 --> 00:01:02.806
Your turn. Say: Built.

20
00:01:05.667 --> 00:01:06.459
Built.

21
00:01:07.217 --> 00:01:08.125
Repaired.

22
00:01:09.117 --> 00:01:10.698
Repaired means fixed.

23
00:01:11.283 --> 00:01:13.039
The road is being repaired.

24
00:01:13.650 --> 00:01:16.535
Your turn. Say: Repaired.

25
00:01:19.400 --> 00:01:20.529
Repaired.

26
00:01:21.283 --> 00:01:22.203
Announce.

27
00:01:23.217 --> 00:01:25.158
Announce means to tell publicly.

28
00:01:25.750 --> 00:01:27.157
They will announce the winner.

29
00:01:27.750 --> 00:01:30.100
Your turn. Say: Announce.

30
00:01:32.967 --> 00:01:33.875
Announce.

31
00:01:34.617 --> 00:01:35.571
Complete.

32
00:01:36.583 --> 00:01:38.130
Complete means to finish.

33
00:01:38.717 --> 00:01:40.414
The task has been completed.

34
00:01:41.017 --> 00:01:43.785
Your turn. Say: Complete.

35
00:01:46.633 --> 00:01:47.495
Complete.

36
00:01:48.250 --> 00:01:49.181
Produce.

37
00:01:50.183 --> 00:01:51.579
Produce means to make.

38
00:01:52.183 --> 00:01:53.858
Rice is produced here.

39
00:01:54.450 --> 00:01:56.940
Your turn. Say: Produce.

40
00:01:59.800 --> 00:02:00.743
Produce.

41
00:02:01.483 --> 00:02:02.438
Discover.

42
00:02:03.450 --> 00:02:05.868
Discover means to find for the first time.

43
00:02:06.483 --> 00:02:09.168
It was discovered in 1950.

44
00:02:09.783 --> 00:02:12.157
Your turn. Say: Discover.

45
00:02:15.000 --> 00:02:15.955
Discover.

46
00:02:16.767 --> 00:02:20.359
Part two: dialogue. Let's listen to a conversation.

47
00:02:21.217 --> 00:02:23.866
Visal, how do I make a passive sentence?

48
00:02:24.950 --> 00:02:33.860
Move the object to the front and use be plus the past participle. The active sentence People grow rice here becomes Rice is grown here.

49
00:02:34.950 --> 00:02:36.671
How do I change the tense?

50
00:02:37.783 --> 00:02:51.279
Change the verb be. Present simple uses is or are, past simple uses was or were, present perfect uses has been or have been, and the future uses will be.

51
00:02:52.383 --> 00:02:54.127
When do I mention the agent?

52
00:02:55.217 --> 00:03:05.311
Use by only when the doer is important or surprising. Otherwise leave it out, as in The bridge was built in 2005.

53
00:03:06.467 --> 00:03:07.851
Part three: grammar.

54
00:03:08.717 --> 00:03:11.854
Grammar focus: be plus past participle.

55
00:03:12.154 --> 00:03:13.434
Look at the pattern.

56
00:03:14.150 --> 00:03:16.150
Rice is grown in this province.

57
00:03:17.050 --> 00:03:19.375
The task has been completed by the team.

58
00:03:20.333 --> 00:03:26.666
Use be in the same tense as the active verb, then add the past participle. Add by only when the doer is important.

59
00:03:27.417 --> 00:03:31.950
Be careful! Don't say: The bridge built in 2005.

60
00:03:33.900 --> 00:03:37.397
Say: The bridge was built in 2005.

61
00:03:37.697 --> 00:03:39.836
Use be + past participle.

62
00:03:40.633 --> 00:03:43.170
Part four: reading. Read and listen.

63
00:03:43.967 --> 00:03:45.084
A New Bridge.

64
00:03:45.384 --> 00:03:48.463
A new bridge was built near our village in 2005.

65
00:03:49.467 --> 00:03:51.756
It is used by farmers every day.

66
00:03:52.767 --> 00:03:54.697
Last year the road was repaired.

67
00:03:55.700 --> 00:03:58.025
A second bridge will be built next year.

68
00:03:59.033 --> 00:04:01.451
The work has been planned by the local council.

69
00:04:02.567 --> 00:04:06.580
Part five: quiz. Five questions. Are you ready?

70
00:04:07.417 --> 00:04:09.567
The passive uses be + blank.

71
00:04:09.867 --> 00:04:13.718
A, past participle. B, base verb. C, -ing.

72
00:04:17.267 --> 00:04:20.149
The answer is A: past participle.

73
00:04:21.283 --> 00:04:23.271
Rice blank in this province.

74
00:04:23.571 --> 00:04:27.329
A, is growing. B, is grown. C, grows.

75
00:04:30.867 --> 00:04:32.820
The answer is B: is grown.

76
00:04:33.983 --> 00:04:35.472
The winner will blank announced.

77
00:04:35.772 --> 00:04:38.659
A, is. B, been. C, be.

78
00:04:42.200 --> 00:04:43.991
The answer is C: be.

79
00:04:45.150 --> 00:04:47.602
The bridge blank built in 2005.

80
00:04:47.902 --> 00:04:50.929
A, was. B, were. C, is.

81
00:04:54.467 --> 00:04:56.257
The answer is A: was.

82
00:04:57.417 --> 00:04:59.962
By + agent is used when the doer is blank.

83
00:05:00.262 --> 00:05:03.532
A, never. B, important. C, unknown.

84
00:05:07.067 --> 00:05:09.507
The answer is B: important.

85
00:05:10.700 --> 00:05:13.724
Part six: speaking. It's your turn to talk.

86
00:05:14.583 --> 00:05:17.535
Change to passive: They will announce the results.

87
00:05:26.350 --> 00:05:27.792
Now listen to Visal.

88
00:05:28.092 --> 00:05:37.876
The results will be announced. I use will be and then the past participle. I do not need to mention they because the doer is not important.

89
00:05:38.176 --> 00:05:39.885
Excellent answer, Visal!

90
00:05:40.783 --> 00:05:45.200
Great work! Now you can use eight new words and be plus past participle.

91
00:05:45.500 --> 00:05:50.521
Today's value is logical rigor. Follow your reasoning wherever it honestly leads.

92
00:05:50.821 --> 00:05:53.148
See you in Unit four. Goodbye!

93
00:05:53.448 --> 00:05:56.112
Thank you, Ms. Emma! Bye, everyone!

